    "notes": "MODEL: owner-FCF component DCF with mid-cycle normalisation (dcf-methods routing: cyclical operating company, owner-fcf.md + adaptations). Fresh build, no prior valuation. FY0 is the trailing twelve months to 30-Sep-2026 so the flows start where the balance sheet stops; year 1 (Oct-26 to Sep-27) contains the guided Q4-2026 trough. EBITDA is defined as operating earnings + DD&A + impairments/idling charges, i.e. AFTER asset-retirement accretion - lower than management's adjusted EBITDA. On that definition: TTM ~1,250 (10.5% margin; 9M-2026 = -505.0 + 900.6 + ~496 of Araxa/Patrocinio/Carlsbad charges), FY2025 ~17%, FY2023-24 ~17-20%, FY2018-20 ~14-19%, FY2021-22 27-30%; the FY2018-25 average is 20.7% including the 2021-22 supercycle and 16.8% excluding it. Base mid-cycle 18.5% sits between. NET DEBT: short-term debt 511.6 + current maturities 68.7 + long-term debt 5,332.8 = 5,913.1 less cash 272.6. BRIDGE: Ma'aden shares at Tadawul fair value added (their mark-to-market is in other income, outside EBITDA); structured accounts payable deducted as debt-like; NCI deducted. ARO (2,529.7 on balance sheet) is charged in the FLOWS, not the bridge: accretion is inside EBITDA and cash spend above accretion (~100/yr) is inside the capex line; the RCRA trusts (~751, restricted to gypstack closure) are therefore left out of the bridge too. Reported FCF is levered (after ~200 of interest paid) and TTM is depressed by the trough plus a working-capital unwind, so last_fcf is not a base to grow from - the forward flows are built from components. Interest income not stripped (net debt, not net cash). Working capital consumes cash on growth (receivables + inventory exceed payables): capture -15%. Price is a regular-session close.",
